#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Cyrus eval report: aggregates run_eval results.jsonl (pure, no network, no model). Spec: matrix.json "scoring".

  python3 report.py <tag|results.jsonl> [<tag2> ...] [--root /root/mbeval] [--baseline FILE] [--save-baseline FILE] [--json]

Several runs given = repeated runs of the SAME matrix: pass@1 / the tables use the first, pass^k (passed in
every run) is added. --baseline compares against an earlier run (a results.jsonl or a --save-baseline file) and
exits 1 when the regression gate fails (a must_refuse pair that regressed, or a required-version final pass
rate that dropped by more than dropPoints). Preview versions are listed separately and never gate.
